1
00:00:08,469 --> 00:00:11,405
One bowl of liquid. A human sees water.

2
00:00:11,485 --> 00:00:17,116
A hungry ghost sees burning pus. A fish
meets its home. A god meets nectar.

3
00:00:17,942 --> 00:00:19,660
Which one is really in the bowl?

4
00:00:20,514 --> 00:00:23,301
I am John Tan, known as Thusness.

5
00:00:23,381 --> 00:00:27,572
These are my own notes, from my
own practice and contemplation.

6
00:00:28,377 --> 00:00:34,377
In Part 1, a human, a bat, a bee and
an ant stood before the same mountain.

7
00:00:34,559 --> 00:00:36,358
Their worlds did not match.

8
00:00:37,165 --> 00:00:40,264
Even so, one belief usually survives.

9
00:00:40,344 --> 00:00:44,164
Surely something is there
underneath. One finished world.

10
00:00:44,244 --> 00:00:47,655
And each creature only sees
it through its own glasses.

11
00:00:47,735 --> 00:00:50,065
One world, many pictures of it.

12
00:00:50,886 --> 00:00:52,998
That belief is what I call the given.

13
00:00:53,805 --> 00:00:55,477
It is not a theory I hold.

14
00:00:55,557 --> 00:00:58,548
It is how things seem, before any thought.

15
00:00:58,628 --> 00:01:01,102
The world is already there, complete.

16
00:01:01,182 --> 00:01:02,982
And seeing only reports it.

17
00:01:03,806 --> 00:01:06,403
So again, I will not argue first.

18
00:01:06,483 --> 00:01:10,805
I will set two ways of seeing
side by side, three more times.

19
00:01:10,885 --> 00:01:12,793
Then we can ask which one holds.

20
00:01:13,667 --> 00:01:14,867
First, a bowl.

21
00:01:16,185 --> 00:01:21,879
Indian and Tibetan philosophers used this
one bowl to bring the question into focus.

22
00:01:21,959 --> 00:01:27,572
A hungry ghost, in their telling, is
a being consumed by craving and lack.

23
00:01:27,652 --> 00:01:30,566
Where I see water, it sees pus and blood.

24
00:01:31,381 --> 00:01:37,143
Surely, then, something sits in the bowl
before any of them looks. Call it H two O.

25
00:01:37,223 --> 00:01:39,480
Bare matter. Neutral stuff.

26
00:01:39,560 --> 00:01:44,308
It is undeniably there, and each kind
of being puts its own glasses on it.

27
00:01:45,126 --> 00:01:49,738
The water is real. The pus and the
nectar are just ways of seeing it.

28
00:01:50,541 --> 00:01:55,017
Or, and it is a big or, look
at how each of these is formed.

29
00:01:55,825 --> 00:02:00,704
The water forms with a human body,
a human thirst, a human tongue.

30
00:02:00,784 --> 00:02:03,054
The pus forms with a ghost's craving.

31
00:02:03,134 --> 00:02:05,586
The home forms with gills and fins.

32
00:02:06,402 --> 00:02:11,254
The thing seen, the one who sees, and
the channel of meeting are designated

33
00:02:11,334 --> 00:02:15,607
together. None of them is a finished
layer underneath the others.

34
00:02:16,438 --> 00:02:20,452
Then what is in the bowl before
anyone meets it? Ask what it is like.

35
00:02:21,253 --> 00:02:24,420
If it has features of
its own, say it is water,

36
00:02:24,500 --> 00:02:26,675
then why does the ghost meet pus?

37
00:02:26,755 --> 00:02:28,636
Its features should show through.

38
00:02:29,441 --> 00:02:33,899
If it has no features at all, then a
featureless something cannot be what any

39
00:02:33,979 --> 00:02:38,613
of them meet. Nothing with no qualities
can set off the taste of water,

40
00:02:38,693 --> 00:02:40,275
or the burn of pus.

41
00:02:41,085 --> 00:02:43,573
A careful mind falls back one step.

42
00:02:43,653 --> 00:02:46,956
Not water, and not pus. Just wetness.

43
00:02:47,036 --> 00:02:48,862
The moisture common to both.

44
00:02:49,694 --> 00:02:52,114
But I have never met wetness on its own.

45
00:02:52,194 --> 00:02:56,720
It only ever shows up as this
drinkable water. This burning pus.

46
00:02:56,800 --> 00:02:58,246
This home for a fish.

47
00:02:59,058 --> 00:03:02,851
Wetness by itself is an idea
drawn from those meetings.

48
00:03:02,931 --> 00:03:04,807
It is not a stuff found under them.

49
00:03:04,887 --> 00:03:08,544
As a working word for comparing
notes, wetness is fine.

50
00:03:08,623 --> 00:03:12,606
As a hidden floor, it is the
old belief in an essence,

51
00:03:12,686 --> 00:03:14,309
wearing new clothes.

52
00:03:15,129 --> 00:03:19,600
And even seen this way, nothing is
missing. I still drink the water.

53
00:03:19,680 --> 00:03:21,629
It still quenches my thirst.

54
00:03:22,442 --> 00:03:24,296
Second, a tick at a pool.

55
00:03:25,110 --> 00:03:29,935
The biologist Jakob von Uexküll showed
that a tick lives in a world of three

56
00:03:30,015 --> 00:03:35,388
signals. The smell of mammal sweat.
The warmth of a body. And hair.

57
00:03:36,189 --> 00:03:39,279
A clear pool of spring
water sends none of them.

58
00:03:40,081 --> 00:03:42,446
Surely the pool is still
there for the tick,

59
00:03:42,526 --> 00:03:44,226
whether it knows it or not.

60
00:03:44,306 --> 00:03:46,346
It is undeniably objective.

61
00:03:46,426 --> 00:03:48,443
The tick is simply blind to it.

62
00:03:49,253 --> 00:03:53,824
Or, and again it is a big or,
look at how the meeting is formed.

63
00:03:54,646 --> 00:03:59,281
The pool has no place in the tick's
world of smell, warmth and hair.

64
00:03:59,361 --> 00:04:02,573
It is not hidden from the
tick. It never forms there.

65
00:04:03,373 --> 00:04:07,844
Yet if the tick falls in, the water
holds it up and carries it away.

66
00:04:07,924 --> 00:04:10,457
So the pool is not nothing
to the tick either.

67
00:04:11,286 --> 00:04:14,848
The tick is cut off from the
channels of sight and recognition.

68
00:04:14,928 --> 00:04:18,833
And it is fully joined to the
water's surface, and its current.

69
00:04:19,666 --> 00:04:22,956
That is the point. Contact
runs along channels.

70
00:04:23,036 --> 00:04:24,645
And it comes in degrees.

71
00:04:25,533 --> 00:04:27,314
Physics shows the same.

72
00:04:27,394 --> 00:04:32,681
Dark matter, as far as anyone can tell,
passes through the Earth without a bump,

73
00:04:32,761 --> 00:04:34,855
because it does not meet light.

74
00:04:34,935 --> 00:04:37,971
Yet the Earth's mass still bends its path.

75
00:04:38,775 --> 00:04:43,224
A neutrino passes through a
wall of lead as if through mist.

76
00:04:43,327 --> 00:04:45,941
For one system, the lead is a wall.

77
00:04:46,058 --> 00:04:48,754
For another, it is almost open space.

78
00:04:49,569 --> 00:04:52,152
Solidity is not stored in the rock.

79
00:04:52,232 --> 00:04:56,309
It is a resistance that forms when two
systems that share the right coupling

80
00:04:56,389 --> 00:04:57,589
meet.

81
00:04:57,962 --> 00:05:02,189
So the choice is not between a hidden
object out there, and nothing at all.

82
00:05:02,269 --> 00:05:07,026
What appears, a wall, a
drink, a burn, or open space,

83
00:05:07,106 --> 00:05:09,042
depends on which channels meet.

84
00:05:09,857 --> 00:05:12,725
And even seen this way,
nothing is missing.

85
00:05:12,805 --> 00:05:17,621
The current still carries the tick,
whether or not the tick ever meets a pool.

86
00:05:18,469 --> 00:05:19,902
Third, the box.

87
00:05:21,001 --> 00:05:23,135
Why does the given feel so certain?

88
00:05:23,215 --> 00:05:27,651
Because underneath the bowl and the
pool sits a picture I rarely notice.

89
00:05:28,482 --> 00:05:31,120
Space is an empty box, ready-made.

90
00:05:31,200 --> 00:05:33,593
I put a solid object in the middle of it.

91
00:05:33,673 --> 00:05:35,359
I put observers around it.

92
00:05:35,439 --> 00:05:39,602
Then each one either sees the
real object, or is fooled.

93
00:05:40,425 --> 00:05:43,307
Surely the box, at least, is given.

94
00:05:43,387 --> 00:05:45,739
It was there before
anything was put in it.

95
00:05:45,819 --> 00:05:48,664
It would still be there if
everything were taken out.

96
00:05:49,477 --> 00:05:54,089
Or, and it is the biggest or, look
at how space itself is formed.

97
00:05:54,905 --> 00:05:59,879
In Einstein's general relativity,
spacetime is not an empty stage.

98
00:05:59,959 --> 00:06:04,041
It is a field that bends with
mass, and moves with energy.

99
00:06:04,845 --> 00:06:10,403
And long before Einstein, Nāgārjuna asked
whether space could exist before its own

100
00:06:10,483 --> 00:06:14,235
mark: the absence of
obstruction. It cannot.

101
00:06:14,315 --> 00:06:17,541
Space and what is in it
are designated together.

102
00:06:18,374 --> 00:06:21,963
Without the box, the puzzle
of the bowl loses its grip.

103
00:06:22,043 --> 00:06:25,713
There is no fixed place where
the one real liquid sits,

104
00:06:25,793 --> 00:06:28,625
waiting to be seen rightly or wrongly.

105
00:06:29,442 --> 00:06:34,729
Space, time, the one who looks, and
what is looked at all come together.

106
00:06:34,809 --> 00:06:36,758
None of them contains the rest.

107
00:06:37,569 --> 00:06:40,423
And even seen this way,
nothing is missing.

108
00:06:40,503 --> 00:06:42,298
I still walk across the room.

109
00:06:42,378 --> 00:06:44,273
The cup is still where I left it.

110
00:06:45,098 --> 00:06:46,298
But we agree.

111
00:06:47,670 --> 00:06:50,077
That is the strongest
reason for the given.

112
00:06:50,157 --> 00:06:52,577
You and I both see water in the bowl.

113
00:06:52,657 --> 00:06:56,843
We name it, pour it, drink
it, and our reports match.

114
00:06:56,923 --> 00:07:00,231
Does that not prove one
real liquid behind us both?

115
00:07:01,029 --> 00:07:04,771
The Indian philosopher
Candrakīrti answered no.

116
00:07:05,569 --> 00:07:09,945
Shared, reliable agreement is
not proof of a hidden floor.

117
00:07:10,025 --> 00:07:12,151
It is what conventional truth is.

118
00:07:12,978 --> 00:07:17,817
Within one kind of being, healthy
senses agree, and correct each other.

119
00:07:17,897 --> 00:07:21,485
A human with jaundice sees a
white conch shell as yellow.

120
00:07:21,565 --> 00:07:23,238
Other humans see it white.

121
00:07:23,318 --> 00:07:27,088
So by human standards, the
jaundiced eye is mistaken.

122
00:07:27,897 --> 00:07:31,010
But the hungry ghost is
not a jaundiced human.

123
00:07:31,090 --> 00:07:35,158
By the standards of its own
kind, its senses work normally.

124
00:07:35,274 --> 00:07:38,433
For it, the liquid
really does work as pus.

125
00:07:39,253 --> 00:07:43,643
Is that circular? Healthy senses are
the ones that agree with the group.

126
00:07:43,723 --> 00:07:46,405
And the group is those
who share the senses.

127
00:07:47,238 --> 00:07:49,237
Yes. It is a circle.

128
00:07:49,317 --> 00:07:54,645
A circle is fatal only if something must
rest on a judge standing outside every

129
00:07:54,725 --> 00:07:57,285
view. No such judge is found.

130
00:07:58,101 --> 00:08:00,942
Inside the circle,
mistakes are still caught.

131
00:08:01,022 --> 00:08:03,184
A second look corrects a misreading.

132
00:08:03,264 --> 00:08:05,548
A healthy eye corrects a jaundiced one.

133
00:08:05,628 --> 00:08:09,316
What the circle rules out is
only a correction from nowhere.

134
00:08:10,142 --> 00:08:13,323
The bowl story did not
begin with Candrakīrti.

135
00:08:13,403 --> 00:08:17,997
Vasubandhu used the ghosts to argue
that there are no outer things at all.

136
00:08:18,077 --> 00:08:23,690
Shared karma, ripening in the mind, is
enough to explain why the ghosts all see

137
00:08:23,770 --> 00:08:25,651
one river of pus.

138
00:08:26,466 --> 00:08:28,741
That makes the mind the floor instead.

139
00:08:29,553 --> 00:08:32,394
Candrakīrti turned the story around.

140
00:08:32,474 --> 00:08:35,587
If the pus is not found
standing on its own,

141
00:08:35,667 --> 00:08:37,856
neither is the mind that sees it.

142
00:08:37,936 --> 00:08:39,898
They rise and fall together.

143
00:08:40,717 --> 00:08:44,604
So the bowl does not prove that
the world is inside the mind.

144
00:08:44,684 --> 00:08:48,522
It shows that neither the world
nor the mind is the floor.

145
00:08:49,337 --> 00:08:52,531
What is left in the bowl, then?
A working reference point.

146
00:08:52,611 --> 00:08:56,213
This bowl is a handy label,
made from the human side.

147
00:08:56,293 --> 00:09:00,113
It lets different beings'
appearances be lined up and compared.

148
00:09:00,193 --> 00:09:04,343
Its job is to coordinate the
views, not to sit underneath them.

149
00:09:05,170 --> 00:09:09,751
Two ways of seeing, three times
over, and agreement tested as well.

150
00:09:09,831 --> 00:09:11,861
Which carries more valid truth?

151
00:09:12,673 --> 00:09:16,981
I test them as I did in Part
1. By experience. By logic.

152
00:09:17,061 --> 00:09:18,575
And by how things work.

153
00:09:19,386 --> 00:09:25,366
By experience. Look into a glass of
water, honestly. What is met? Coolness.

154
00:09:25,446 --> 00:09:28,618
Clearness. Wetness on the lip. The name.

155
00:09:29,433 --> 00:09:32,369
At no point do I meet a
neutral liquid behind them.

156
00:09:32,449 --> 00:09:35,820
One that is neither my
water, nor the fish's home,

157
00:09:35,900 --> 00:09:37,518
nor the ghost's pus.

158
00:09:37,598 --> 00:09:40,825
That liquid is never
found. It is supplied.

159
00:09:41,629 --> 00:09:45,978
Then turn around, and look for a
mind holding the water inside it.

160
00:09:46,058 --> 00:09:49,610
That is not found either.
Mind and object come together.

161
00:09:50,430 --> 00:09:53,869
By logic. A given world would
have to be like something.

162
00:09:53,949 --> 00:09:58,652
If it has features, they should show
through to every being. They do not.

163
00:09:58,732 --> 00:10:02,406
If it has none, it cannot
set off any meeting at all.

164
00:10:03,213 --> 00:10:08,731
A self-standing wetness, or matter,
undoes itself the moment it is picked out.

165
00:10:08,811 --> 00:10:12,345
Picking it out needs contrast,
a channel and a name.

166
00:10:12,425 --> 00:10:15,094
The very dependencies
it was meant to escape.

167
00:10:15,926 --> 00:10:16,865
By working.

168
00:10:16,945 --> 00:10:21,960
The given view says the world is orderly
because something solid underneath holds

169
00:10:22,040 --> 00:10:24,963
it steady. But what is
fixed cannot change.

170
00:10:25,043 --> 00:10:27,223
And what cannot change cannot act.

171
00:10:28,050 --> 00:10:30,728
The formed view explains
the working fully.

172
00:10:30,808 --> 00:10:32,608
Barley seeds grow barley.

173
00:10:32,711 --> 00:10:35,593
Fire burns. The current carries the tick.

174
00:10:35,673 --> 00:10:37,712
Humans agree that this is water.

175
00:10:37,792 --> 00:10:42,454
These are dependently arisen patterns,
meeting other patterns reliably,

176
00:10:42,534 --> 00:10:44,320
along shared channels.

177
00:10:45,129 --> 00:10:46,779
Order never needed a floor.

178
00:10:47,701 --> 00:10:51,439
So the given is not the truer
view. It is the default one.

179
00:10:51,519 --> 00:10:54,509
It carries the weight of
habit, and of language.

180
00:10:54,589 --> 00:11:00,016
The noun, the bowl, quietly sets
up one object behind every view.

181
00:11:00,846 --> 00:11:04,331
The formed view carries
experience and logic both.

182
00:11:05,133 --> 00:11:07,987
None of this makes my
everyday claims false.

183
00:11:08,067 --> 00:11:09,713
The water is water.

184
00:11:09,793 --> 00:11:12,376
I still drink it, and I still say so.

185
00:11:12,456 --> 00:11:16,778
What fails is only the extra
claim: a finished world underneath,

186
00:11:16,858 --> 00:11:18,237
waiting to be seen.

187
00:11:19,057 --> 00:11:21,739
And one thing matters
more than the argument.

188
00:11:22,541 --> 00:11:25,749
If the ghost's pus is
truly pus for the ghost,

189
00:11:25,829 --> 00:11:31,306
its suffering is not an optical mistake,
to be waved away from the human side.

190
00:11:31,386 --> 00:11:33,996
No single view owns the real world.

191
00:11:34,076 --> 00:11:37,452
So no being's lived world
can be brushed aside.

192
00:11:38,278 --> 00:11:41,935
Seeing through the given takes
nothing away from another's pain.

193
00:11:42,015 --> 00:11:43,705
Or from the wish to ease it.

194
00:11:44,509 --> 00:11:47,816
This is Part 2 of the
Dependent Arising series.

195
00:11:48,617 --> 00:11:54,080
In Part 3, Measured, or Formed, I
take the same question into physics.

196
00:11:54,160 --> 00:11:58,741
Surely a measurement, at least,
reads a world that is already there.

197
00:11:58,821 --> 00:12:02,205
I set two physicists
beside dependent arising,

198
00:12:02,285 --> 00:12:06,526
Carlo Rovelli and Karen Barad,
and show where they echo it,

199
00:12:06,606 --> 00:12:08,120
and where I part from them.

